OL,3,GNEWSADisabled riding charity fears
OL,4,Afuture over access row
OL,5,
OL,6,FA charity which provides horse riding
OL,7,Ffor disabled children says it fears for
OL,8,Fits future because of a dispute over
OL,9,Ffootpaths on its land.
OL,11,FThe Avon Centre in Bristol, has spent
OL,12,Fmore than 40 years helping disabled and
OL,13,Fvulnerable children and adults through
OL,14,Fhorse riding and outdoor activities.
OL,16,FIt says a bid to create public rights
OL,17,Fof way across its woodland could create
OL,18,Fsafety risks for riders, horses and
OL,19,Fvolunteers: "It's an enormous threat to
OL,20,Fwhat we do," said therapeutic
OL,21,Factivities programme manager Kim
OL,22,FLangbridge.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
